00:00:02.670 --> 00:00:04.469 align:start position:0%
we have been working very hard since  Monday morning to come to an agreement  on the 2018 catch limits for the main  commercial fish stocks in the EU waters  and for EU fishing vessels in non EU  waters the negotiations have been  difficult but I am very pleased to  announce that the council has arrived at  a unanimous agreement with just one  member state abstaining we paid  particular attention to the European  Eagle stock which as you know is in a  critical condition all the Member States  committed to improve implementation of  the real management plans we are also  making additional efforts to protect sea  bass a very important stock for many  countries for the first time at a low  level  we agreed to close eel fisheries for  three months during their migration  period  moreover Member States committed two  additional actions to protect the Eels  throughout its lifecycle and in all sea  basins today we agreed on fishing  opportunities worth over five billion  euros benefiting more than 50 thousand  fishermen as a result of responsible  decisions in the last year's the  economic performance of the youth fleet  has improved considerably and its  profits are increasing
 

